regulatory approval is expensive, often takes many years and can vary substantially based upon the type, complexity and novelty of the products involved,
as well as the target indications and patient population. Approval policies or regulations may change, and the regulatory authorities have substantial
discretion in the drug approval process, including the ability to delay, limit or deny approval of a product candidate for many reasons. Despite the time and
expense invested in clinical development of product candidates, regulatory approval is never guaranteed.
